  "tradeoffs": [
    "Rust has less free general heap than the optimized native implementation: about 29.5 kB versus 37.7 kB in these trials, while improving from about 15.2 kB before this work. Task stacks were not reduced to obtain the FPS gain.",
    "Frames are forced full-screen redraws; normal dirty-region updates can have different throughput. These results do not assert a frame rate for every operating scenario."
  ],
  "changes": [
    "Single native 25 Hz barometer producer; one conversion publishes a coherent cross-core snapshot; UI never performs I2C sampling.",
    "Disable cc helper default PIC on ESP-IDF for LVGL/libcanard; host PIC remains enabled.",
    "Use the ESP-IDF allocator for LVGL instead of reserving a second 48 KiB arena; Rust owns a stable four-byte-aligned 64-row draw buffer.",
    "Bound numeric formatting on the UI stack, reuse alert-ID storage, avoid copying maintenance buffers under the UI/control shared mutex.",
    "Abort explicitly on LVGL allocation failure and reject non-finite sea-pressure settings.",
    "Run C rendering boundaries with AddressSanitizer/leak detection in CI; preserve screen goldens and existing protocol/emulator tests."
  ],
  "rejected_experiments": [
    "-O2 LVGL with the small buffer was slower than size optimization on this board.",
    "-O3 Rust/LVGL was slower and left less free heap.",
    "Keeping the fixed LVGL arena while moving the larger buffer into it exhausted the host test arena; the final implementation shares the IDF allocator instead."
